# Uploaded to EAS Build; anything listed here is left out of the build context.

# THE LOCKFILE IS EXCLUDED ON PURPOSE.
#
# EAS installs with `npm ci` when a lockfile is present, and npm cannot
# generate a lockfile for this dependency graph that its own `npm ci` accepts.
# Reproduced repeatedly from a clean cache: a lockfile written by `npm install`
# is rejected seconds later by `npm ci` with "Missing: X from lock file" —
# @opentelemetry/core, @aws-cdk/toolkit-lib, archiver. The conflict lives
# entirely inside @aws-amplify/backend-cli's CDK tree: two versions of
# @aws-cdk/toolkit-lib are required, npm writes only the hoisted one.
#
# Without the lockfile the builder runs `npm install`, which resolves fine.
# The cost is that builds are not byte-reproducible.
#
# The real fix is to move the Amplify BACKEND tooling out of the app's
# package.json — it is only used by `ampx` to deploy, and the mobile app never
# imports it. That is a restructure, not a one-liner, and it is the thing to do
# before this app has more than one person building it.
package-lock.json

# Not needed on the builder, and large.
supabase/
docs/
store/
scripts/
.amplify/
dist/
